      "content": "No, no, I'm not talking about the mythical creatures, just a bit of a... let's say, a \"goblin-like\" chaos that can ensue during peak travel times. But, I digress.\n\nRegarding your luggage, Eurostar allows one piece of checked luggage and one piece of carry-on luggage per passenger. So, with two large suitcases and a carry-on, you're within the limit. However, if you have any additional items, such as a personal item or a musical instrument, you'll need to check with Eurostar to see if there are any additional fees or restrictions.\n\nIt's worth noting that if you have a lot of luggage, you might want to consider checking in online and printing or downloading your boarding pass, as I mentioned earlier. This can help speed up the check-in process and reduce the likelihood of any... goblin-like delays.\n\nAlso, keep in mind that if you have any fragile or special items, you might want to consider packing them in a protective case or bag to avoid any... unpleasantness.",
